[{:db/id 17592186100920 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c4c74154-74a4-59d0-b3a0-d5c61e076d93" "question-d8305832-8106-52c2-97f7-863006f292f6" "question-5bb65209-2ef4-5e75-8f8a-170aaa43e597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100827 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2c1d20bb-7423-5d1e-aef5-963d443861a9" "question-d746f1cc-0701-523c-a4d0-da44e37048c9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100919 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-185be666-6314-550d-b382-232010c7dadf" "question-c69fac4d-ae7b-5cea-a5ac-be4dd3c238bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" "question-33fa495c-c75d-54c3-993a-6917944aba8b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101439 :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(1)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(1)=-3,\\,g(1)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(1)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=1$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=1} & =f(1){g}^{′}(1)+g(1){f}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186099795 :answer-field/correct 17592186099796 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4c74154-74a4-59d0-b3a0-d5c61e076d93" :question/id #uuid "c4c74154-74a4-59d0-b3a0-d5c61e076d93" :question/math-academy-id "q-311275" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=2.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2} & =f(2){g}^{′}(2)+g(2){f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =(4)(5)+(-3)(2) \\\\  & =20-6 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8f3259cf-2393-5330-8b72-85edb30bad40"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8f3259cf-2393-5330-8b72-85edb30bad40" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f3259cf-2393-5330-8b72-85edb30bad40" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1504691b-9c8e-514b-813d-d8d819372de8" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1504691b-9c8e-514b-813d-d8d819372de8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1504691b-9c8e-514b-813d-d8d819372de8" :answer/id #uuid "1504691b-9c8e-514b-813d-d8d819372de8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8305832-8106-52c2-97f7-863006f292f6" :question/id #uuid "d8305832-8106-52c2-97f7-863006f292f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340450" :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $\\sqrt{2}$ | $-5$ | $-\\sqrt{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4} & =f(4){g}^{′}(4)+g(4){f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2})(\\frac{1}{2})+(-5)(-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+5\\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{11\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-aa311fea-d368-5050-baa1-a2dc9ec6a320"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-aa311fea-d368-5050-baa1-a2dc9ec6a320" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa311fea-d368-5050-baa1-a2dc9ec6a320" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ec766d22-6e91-58e7-a9c1-9af8ac5b1ef1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ec766d22-6e91-58e7-a9c1-9af8ac5b1ef1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ec766d22-6e91-58e7-a9c1-9af8ac5b1ef1" :answer/id #uuid "ec766d22-6e91-58e7-a9c1-9af8ac5b1ef1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5bb65209-2ef4-5e75-8f8a-170aaa43e597" :question/id #uuid "5bb65209-2ef4-5e75-8f8a-170aaa43e597" :question/math-academy-id "q-340986" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-2)=-3,\\,{f}^{′}(-2)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,g(-2)=4,\\,{g}^{′}(-2)=-2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=-2.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=-2} & =f(-2){g}^{′}(-2)+g(-2){f}^{′}(-2) \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c82e7a9c-8dab-5491-8b1e-06a499a120d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c82e7a9c-8dab-5491-8b1e-06a499a120d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c82e7a9c-8dab-5491-8b1e-06a499a120d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d54946b5-2086-5260-a777-bae8c0647b93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d54946b5-2086-5260-a777-bae8c0647b93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d54946b5-2086-5260-a777-bae8c0647b93" :answer/id #uuid "d54946b5-2086-5260-a777-bae8c0647b93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2c1d20bb-7423-5d1e-aef5-963d443861a9" :question/id #uuid "2c1d20bb-7423-5d1e-aef5-963d443861a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-341022" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,{f}^{′}(-1)=\\sqrt{3},\\,g(-1)=-3,\\,{g}^{′}(-1)=2\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=-1.$ Do not round the answer. \n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=-1,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=-1} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(-1)g(-1)-f(-1){g}^{′}(-1)}{(g(-1))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (-3)-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (2)}{(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3}}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8031ab93-01cf-54ec-b7bc-990d2a3d5cb2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8031ab93-01cf-54ec-b7bc-990d2a3d5cb2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8031ab93-01cf-54ec-b7bc-990d2a3d5cb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-884462d0-f054-5127-a5a7-5d262d07f786" :answer-field/choices ["answer-884462d0-f054-5127-a5a7-5d262d07f786"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-884462d0-f054-5127-a5a7-5d262d07f786" :answer/id #uuid "884462d0-f054-5127-a5a7-5d262d07f786" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d746f1cc-0701-523c-a4d0-da44e37048c9" :question/id #uuid "d746f1cc-0701-523c-a4d0-da44e37048c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-341023" :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(0)=3,\\,{f}^{′}(0)=2,\\,g(0)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,{g}^{′}(0)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=0.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{(g(0))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot (\\frac{1}{2})-3\\cdot (-1)}{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3}{\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd3d39f4-7fca-54a5-b577-33373150e47b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd3d39f4-7fca-54a5-b577-33373150e47b" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd3d39f4-7fca-54a5-b577-33373150e47b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-d2a6da88-9576-56b0-8a8b-0b3fdf247a1d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d2a6da88-9576-56b0-8a8b-0b3fdf247a1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2a6da88-9576-56b0-8a8b-0b3fdf247a1d" :answer/id #uuid "d2a6da88-9576-56b0-8a8b-0b3fdf247a1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-185be666-6314-550d-b382-232010c7dadf" :question/id #uuid "185be666-6314-550d-b382-232010c7dadf" :question/math-academy-id "q-72997" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=7$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $z(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${z}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $7$ | $-4$ | $-6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))$ at $x=7.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))=4{q}^{′}(x)-3{z}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=7$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4q(x)-3z(x))|}_{x=7} & =4{q}^{′}(7)-3{z}^{′}(7) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 8-3\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =32-30 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dea2d52c-4b8d-5f8a-924d-94f5b86236d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dea2d52c-4b8d-5f8a-924d-94f5b86236d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "dea2d52c-4b8d-5f8a-924d-94f5b86236d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f76df83f-5d24-5d40-b3c4-b3af286d8e47" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f76df83f-5d24-5d40-b3c4-b3af286d8e47" "answer-38698b4e-d44f-55f7-83f8-ecd53c147223" "answer-37431c2f-97b6-5e35-938b-ebdf9e1e817f" "answer-53c4756c-c15a-5fbd-8706-90ef2f70a497" "answer-f019caa9-35f2-5128-873a-d2a0bef29a2b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f76df83f-5d24-5d40-b3c4-b3af286d8e47" :answer/id #uuid "f76df83f-5d24-5d40-b3c4-b3af286d8e47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38698b4e-d44f-55f7-83f8-ecd53c147223" :answer/id #uuid "38698b4e-d44f-55f7-83f8-ecd53c147223" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37431c2f-97b6-5e35-938b-ebdf9e1e817f" :answer/id #uuid "37431c2f-97b6-5e35-938b-ebdf9e1e817f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53c4756c-c15a-5fbd-8706-90ef2f70a497" :answer/id #uuid "53c4756c-c15a-5fbd-8706-90ef2f70a497" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f019caa9-35f2-5128-873a-d2a0bef29a2b" :answer/id #uuid "f019caa9-35f2-5128-873a-d2a0bef29a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-c69fac4d-ae7b-5cea-a5ac-be4dd3c238bf" :question/id #uuid "c69fac4d-ae7b-5cea-a5ac-be4dd3c238bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-72991" :question/problem "The values of functions $q(x)$ and $r(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $q(x)$ | $r(x)$ | ${q}^{′}(x)$ | ${r}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $-5$ | $3$ | $4$ | $-7$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))$ at $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))=2{q}^{′}(x)+3{r}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2q(x)+3r(x))|}_{x=4} & =2{q}^{′}(4)+3{r}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =8-21 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-207ed61a-0df3-5930-bbce-d91cf163a8aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-207ed61a-0df3-5930-bbce-d91cf163a8aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "207ed61a-0df3-5930-bbce-d91cf163a8aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-dbed82e4-7c5a-561f-b1c0-d6a883be7988" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dbed82e4-7c5a-561f-b1c0-d6a883be7988" "answer-2742eed6-e955-5ad7-b7bb-8036b69a6c7a" "answer-618e9096-014a-5923-a974-dd28dce5f6a1" "answer-b8500a3e-6caa-51ce-82aa-75e017302f20" "answer-e244cba0-96e8-5a3e-b12e-9f3e21904ba8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dbed82e4-7c5a-561f-b1c0-d6a883be7988" :answer/id #uuid "dbed82e4-7c5a-561f-b1c0-d6a883be7988" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2742eed6-e955-5ad7-b7bb-8036b69a6c7a" :answer/id #uuid "2742eed6-e955-5ad7-b7bb-8036b69a6c7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-618e9096-014a-5923-a974-dd28dce5f6a1" :answer/id #uuid "618e9096-014a-5923-a974-dd28dce5f6a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8500a3e-6caa-51ce-82aa-75e017302f20" :answer/id #uuid "b8500a3e-6caa-51ce-82aa-75e017302f20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e244cba0-96e8-5a3e-b12e-9f3e21904ba8" :answer/id #uuid "e244cba0-96e8-5a3e-b12e-9f3e21904ba8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101532 :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $3$ | $1$ | $4$ | $2$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{f(x)+1}{2g(x)},$ compute ${h}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=f(x)+1$ and $v=2g(x).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2{g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot 2g(x)-(f(x)+1)\\cdot 2{g}^{′}(x)}{{(2g(x))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-2{g}^{′}(x)(f(x)+1)}{4{g}^{2}(x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-{g}^{′}(x)(f(x)+1)}{2{g}^{2}(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(2)g(2)-{g}^{′}(2)(f(2)+1)}{2{g}^{2}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1-2(3+1)}{2\\cdot {1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186100353 :answer-field/correct 17592186100358 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" :question/id #uuid "820989f9-6d7d-594e-a9c9-c00397b747b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-311283" :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=3$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $-2$ | $6$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2+h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute  ${f}^{′}(3).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(3)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2+h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}={h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{{h}^{′}(t)z(t)-(2+h(t)){z}^{′}(t)}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=3,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =\\frac{{h}^{′}(3)z(3)-(2+h(3)){z}^{′}(3)}{{z}^{2}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 6-(2+(-2))(-1)}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30-(0)(-1)}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{36} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-72717550-a6aa-5a9b-8df2-1401d5e8c09c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-72717550-a6aa-5a9b-8df2-1401d5e8c09c" :answer-field/id #uuid "72717550-a6aa-5a9b-8df2-1401d5e8c09c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/id #uuid "cc13996b-ed1b-5e8e-a207-d62c584e1725" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-33fa495c-c75d-54c3-993a-6917944aba8b" :question/id #uuid "33fa495c-c75d-54c3-993a-6917944aba8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-341455" :question/problem "For the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\np(5)=-2,\\,{p}^{′}(5)=3,\\,q(5)=1,\\,{q}^{′}(5)=-4\n$$\n\nIf $z(x)=(p(x)+2q(x))(3-p(x)),$ compute ${z}^{′}(5).$\n\n${z}^{′}(5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=p(x)+2q(x)$ and $v=3-p(x).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-{p}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(p(x)+2q(x))(-{p}^{′}(x))+(3-p(x))({p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =-{p}^{′}(x)(p(x)+2q(x))+(3-p(x))({p}^{′}(x)+2{q}^{′}(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(5) & =-{p}^{′}(5)(p(5)+2q(5))+(3-p(5))({p}^{′}(5)+2{q}^{′}(5)) \\\\  & =-(3)(-2+2\\cdot 1)+(3-(-2))(3+2\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-627417ee-d344-525b-a022-34e240f3b475"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-627417ee-d344-525b-a022-34e240f3b475" :answer-field/id #uuid "627417ee-d344-525b-a022-34e240f3b475" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e2774d8c-2b07-5fa2-a4bb-4192356d8dfa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e2774d8c-2b07-5fa2-a4bb-4192356d8dfa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e2774d8c-2b07-5fa2-a4bb-4192356d8dfa" :answer/id #uuid "e2774d8c-2b07-5fa2-a4bb-4192356d8dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101450 :question/problem "For the functions $h(x)$ and $z(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nh(5)=5,\\,{h}^{′}(5)=-3,\\,z(5)=-6,\\,{z}^{′}(5)=8\n$$\n\nIf $w(x)=(h(x)+z(x))(3h(x)-10)$, compute ${w}^{′}(5).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=h(x)+z(x)$ and $v=3h(x)-10.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3{h}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =({h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x))(3h(x)-10)+(h(x)+z(x))(3{h}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =({h}^{′}(x)+{z}^{′}(x))(3h(x)-10)+3{h}^{′}(x)(h(x)+z(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}^{′}(5) & =({h}^{′}(5)+{z}^{′}(5))(3h(5)-10)+3{h}^{′}(5)(h(5)+z(5)) \\\\  & =(-3+8)\\cdot (3\\cdot 5-10)+3\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (5+(-6)) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 5+3\\cdot (-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186099861 :answer-field/correct 17592186099863 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101942 :tutorial/content "Let's suppose we only know the values of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ at $x=0$ along with their derivatives, as given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\nCan we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big )$ at $x=0?$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) = f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) \\right|_{x=0}\t=\tf'(0)g(0)+f(0)g'(0).\n$$\n\nAll of these values are given in the table! So, substituting the values from the table into the formula, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & ={f}^{′}(0)g(0)+f(0){g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186101089 :activity/expected-seconds 960.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
